<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Gray-Day.jpg" alt="Plein air painting at Golden Gardens Park" width="550" height="417" data-filename="Gray Day.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Gray Day. 9x12, oil and cold wax on linen panel. 2016.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Rapidly changing conditions and lack of light made for difficult painting conditions today.&nbsp;<span style="line-height: 1.42857;">In retrospect, the cold wax medium also made the painting harder to execute.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">There's something about this season that can make overcast gray skies feel very muddy.</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">&nbsp;In order to avoid making the painting too dull,&nbsp;</span>I used the Ned Jacob palette (ultramarine, alizarin, cad orange, cad yellow medium). That allowed me to create a large range of<span style="line-height: 1.42857;">&nbsp;grays&nbsp;</span><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">and made it easier to manage temperature shifts in the masses.</span></p>
